Fix the Google authentication start request so it uses the public, bodyless
Follei endpoint and does not create an unnecessary CORS preflight.

Current origins:
- Frontend: http://localhost:5173
- Backend: http://127.0.0.1:8000

The backend public endpoint is:

POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/google/start

It accepts a completely empty request:
- no Authorization header
- no Content-Type header
- no Cache-Control request header
- no request body
- no cookies or credentials

Change authApi.ts to this exact behavior:

export async function startGoogleAuth(): Promise<GoogleAuthStartResponse> {
  const response = await fetch(
    `${API_BASE_URL}/api/v1/auth/google/start`,
    {
      method: "POST",
      cache: "no-store",
      credentials: "omit"
    }
  );

  let payload: unknown;

  try {
    payload = await response.json();
  } catch {
    throw new Error(`Google authentication returned HTTP ${response.status}`);
  }

  if (!response.ok) {
    const detail =
      typeof payload === "object" &&
      payload !== null &&
      "detail" in payload &&
      typeof payload.detail === "string"
        ? payload.detail
        : "Could not start Google authentication";

    throw new Error(detail);
  }

  return payload as GoogleAuthStartResponse;
}

Important distinctions:

- `cache: "no-store"` is a Fetch API option.
- Do not manually send the HTTP request header `Cache-Control: no-store`.
- Do not send `Content-Type: application/json` when there is no JSON body.
- Do not send `body: JSON.stringify({})`.
- Do not use the shared authenticated Axios client for this public endpoint.
- Do not send an Authorization header.
- Do not set `credentials: "include"`.
- Do not call `/api/v1/integrations/google-workspace/oauth/start`.

Remove code resembling:

headers: {
  "Content-Type": "application/json",
  "Cache-Control": "no-store"
},
body: JSON.stringify({})

The public start request should be bodyless. That makes it a simple cross-origin
POST and avoids the OPTIONS preflight entirely.

After receiving the response, validate:

payload.data.flow === "account_auth"
payload.data.requires_bearer === false
payload.data.authorization_url starts with
"https://accounts.google.com/"

Then perform:

window.location.replace(payload.data.authorization_url);

Keep the existing useRef double-click guard.

The callback exchange remains JSON:

POST /api/v1/auth/google/exchange
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exchange_code": "..."
}

That endpoint may use CORS preflight; the backend supports it.

Do not report success based only on TypeScript compilation. Open the browser
Network panel and verify:

1. Google start produces one POST request.
2. The POST returns HTTP 200.
3. No OPTIONS request is made for Google start.
4. The POST request has no Authorization header.
5. The POST request has no Content-Type or Cache-Control request header.
6. The response includes:
   Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5173
7. Browser navigates to accounts.google.com.